   [--device DEVICE [DEVICE ...]] [--optimizer OPTIMIZER]\n               [--nesterov NESTEROV] [--batch-size BATCH_SIZE]\n               [--test-batch-size TEST_BATCH_SIZE] [--start-epoch START_EPOCH]\n               [--num-epoch NUM_EPOCH] [--weight-decay WEIGHT_DECAY]\n               [--lr-decay-rate LR_DECAY_RATE] [--warm_up_epoch WARM_UP_EPOCH]\n\nSpatial Temporal Graph Convolution Network\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --work-dir WORK_DIR   the work folder for storing results\n  -model_saved_name MODEL_SAVED_NAME\n  --config CONFIG       path to the configuration file\n  --phase PHASE         must be train or test\n  --save-score SAVE_SCORE\n                        if ture, the classification score will be stored\n  --seed SEED           random seed for pytorch\n  --log-interval LOG_INTERVAL\n                        the interval for printing messages (#iteration)\n  --save-interval SAVE_INTERVAL\n                        the interval for storing models (#iteration)\n  --save-epoch SAVE_EPOCH\n                        the start epoch to save model (#iteration)\n  --eval-interval EVAL_INTERVAL\n                        the interval for evaluating models (#iteration)\n  --print-log PRINT_LOG\n                        print logging or not\n  --show-topk SHOW_TOPK [SHOW_TOPK ...]\n                        which Top K accuracy will be shown\n  --feeder FEEDER       data loader will be used\n  --num-worker NUM_WORKER\n                        the number of worker for data loader\n  --train-feeder-args TRAIN_FEEDER_ARGS\n                        the arguments of data loader for training\n  --test-feeder-args TEST_FEEDER_ARGS\n                        the arguments of data loader for test\n  --model MODEL         the model will be used\n  --model-args MODEL_ARGS\n                        the arguments of model\n  --weights WEIGHTS     the weights for network initialization\n  --ignore-weights IGNORE_WEIGHTS [IGNORE_WEIGHTS ...]\n                        the name of weights which will be ignored in the\n                        initialization\n  --base-lr BASE_LR     initial learning rate\n  --step STEP [STEP ...]\n                        the epoch where optimizer reduce the learning rate\n  --device DEVICE [DEVICE ...]\n                        the indexes of GPUs for training or testing\n  --optimizer OPTIMIZER\n                        type of optimizer\n  --nesterov NESTEROV   use nesterov or not\n  --batch-size BATCH_SIZE\n                        training batch size\n  --test-batch-size TEST_BATCH_SIZE\n                        test batch size\n  --start-epoch START_EPOCH\n                        start training from which epoch\n  --num-epoch NUM_EPOCH\n                        stop training in which epoch\n  --weight-decay WEIGHT_DECAY\n                        weight decay for optimizer\n  --lr-decay-rate LR_DECAY_RATE\n                        decay rate for learning rate\n  --warm_up_epoch WARM_UP_EPOCH\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":18},{"cell_type":"code","source":"!grep -n -A20 \"Testing\" README.md","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-27T18:19:21.593207Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-27T18:19:21.593650Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-27T18:19:21.733465Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-27T18:19:21.593603Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-27T18:19:21.732150Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"76:# Training & Testing\n77-\n78-### Training\n79-\n80-- Change the config file depending on what you want.\n81-\n82-```\n83-# Example: training CTRGCN on NTU RGB+D 120 cross subject with GPU 0\n84-python main.py --config config/nturgbd120-cross-subject/default.yaml --work-dir work_dir/ntu120/csub/ctrgcn --device 0\n85-# Example: training provided baseline on NTU RGB+D 120 cross subject\n86-python main.py --config config/nturgbd120-cross-subject/default.yaml --model model.baseline.Model--work-dir work_dir/ntu120/csub/baseline --device 0\n87-```\n88-\n89-- To train model on NTU RGB+D 60/120 with bone or motion modalities, setting `bone` or `vel` arguments in the config file `default.yaml` or in the command line.\n90-\n91-```\n92-# Example: training CTRGCN on NTU RGB+D 120 cross subject under bone modality\n93-python main.py --config config/nturgbd120-cross-subject/default.yaml --train_feeder_args bone=True --test_feeder_args bone=True --work-dir work_dir/ntu120/csub/ctrgcn_bone --device 0\n94-```\n95-\n96-- To train model on NW-UCLA with bone or motion modalities, you need to modify `data_path` in `train_feeder_args` and `test_feeder_args` to \"bone\" or \"motion\" or \"bone motion\", and run\n--\n109:### Testing\n110-\n111-- To test the trained models saved in <work_dir>, run the following command:\n112-\n113-```\n114-python main.py --config <work_dir>/config.yaml --work-dir <work_dir> --phase test --save-score True --weights <work_dir>/xxx.pt --device 0\n115-```\n116-\n117-- To ensemble the results of different modalities, run \n118-```\n119-# Example: ensemble four modalities of CTRGCN on NTU RGB+D 120 cross subject\n120-python ensemble.py --datasets ntu120/xsub --joint-dir work_dir/ntu120/csub/ctrgcn --bone-dir work_dir/ntu120/csub/ctrgcn_bone --joint-motion-dir work_dir/ntu120/csub/ctrgcn_motion --bone-motion-dir work_dir/ntu120/csub/ctrgcn_bone_motion\n121-```\n122-\n123-### Pretrained Models\n124-\n125-- Download pretrained models for producing the final results on NTU RGB+D 60&120 cross subject [[Google Drive]](https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1C9XUAgnwrGelvl4mGGVZQW6akiapgdnd?usp=sharing).\n126:- Put files to <work_dir> and run **Testing** command to produce the final result.\n127-\n128-## Acknowledgements\n129-\n130-This repo is based on [2s-AGCN](https://github.com/lshiwjx/2s-AGCN). The data processing is borrowed from [SGN](https://github.com/microsoft/SGN) and [HCN](https://github.com/huguyuehuhu/HCN-pytorch).\n131-\n132-Thanks to the original authors for their work!\n133-\n134-# Citation\n135-\n136-Please cite this work if you find it useful:.\n137-\n138-      @inproceedings{chen2021channel,\n139-        title={Channel-wise Topology Refinement Graph Convolution for Skeleton-Based Action Recognition},\n140-        author={Chen, Yuxin and Zhang, Ziqi and Yuan, Chunfeng and Li, Bing and Deng, Ying and Hu, Weiming},\n141-        booktitle={Proceedings of the IEEE/CVF International Conference on Computer Vision},\n142-        pages={13359--13368},\n143-        year={2021}\n144-      }\n145-\n146-# Contact\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":19},{"cell_type":"code","source":"!find /kaggle/working/CTR-GCN/pretrained_model/NTU60_Xsub/CTRGCN_joint_89.9 -maxdepth 2 -type f","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-27T18:20:37.556934Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-27T18:20:37.557340Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-27T18:20:37.693834Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-27T18:20:37.557298Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-27T18:20:37.692553Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"/kaggle/working/CTR-GCN/pretrained_model/NTU60_Xsub/CTRGCN_joint_89.9/runs-60-37560.pt\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":21},{"cell_type":"code","source":"%cd /kaggle/working/CTR-GCN\n\n!python main.py \\\n    --config config/nturgbd-cross-subject/default.yaml \\\n    --phase test \\\n    --weights pretrained_model/NTU60_Xsub/CTRGCN_joint_89.9/runs-60-37560.pt \\\n    --device 0 \\\n    --save-score True","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-27T18:22:02.095271Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-27T18:22:02.095811Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-27T18:22:15.003522Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-27T18:22:02.095766Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-27T18:22:15.002164Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"/kaggle/working/CTR-GCN\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/kaggle/working/CTR-GCN/main.py\", line 573, in <module>\n    default_arg = yaml.load(f)\n                  ^^^^^^^^^^^^\nTypeEr